Danielle, 39 – Severe Flu

“I had the flu about a year ago and it was honestly one of the worst times I’ve been sick. It didn’t start off that bad, just a sore throat and feeling kind of tired, so I ignored it at first. I still went to work, still ran errands, and didn’t really think much of it. But within a day or two, it got way worse. I had a high fever, chills, and my whole body felt sore like I couldn’t even move without it hurting.

What really made it worse is that I didn’t stop when I should have. I kept trying to push through, and I think that made my recovery longer. Eventually I had no choice but to stay home because I literally didn’t have the energy to do anything. I spent most of my time in bed, sleeping and trying to drink water even when I didn’t feel like it.

One thing I learned from that experience is that your body gives you signs early on, and ignoring them just makes everything worse. If I had stayed home sooner, rested more, and taken it seriously earlier, I probably wouldn’t have gotten as bad as I did.

Advice:

Don’t ignore early symptoms just because they seem small
Rest as soon as you start feeling sick, not later
Drink fluids even if you don’t feel like it
Stay home so you don’t spread it to others

Now, anytime I feel even slightly sick, I slow down immediately instead of trying to “fight through it.” It’s honestly not worth it.”
